  "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${A}^{T}=A$\n- ${A}^{2}=A$\n- $A$ is an orthogonal projection matrix",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that $Q$ is an orthogonal projection matrix if and only if ${Q}^{2}=Q$ and ${Q}^{T}=Q.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since ${A}^{T}\\ne A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false since not both statements I and II are true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only.\"",
